# runcc — the RATE leg under the 256 MiB floor, A/B in one cluster, 2026-09-06
# arm A = drill-02f251b8 (floor 0), arm B = drill-94b2965d (floor 256 MiB + the exemption + the cadence from the LIST)
# each arm: a seed, two 64 MiB pushes (so a base exists), then P2 = 32 pushers x 60 s of tiny commits to distinct branches, three times

pushes/s by repetition (32 pushers, 60 s each, the repository carrying every previous rep's branches):
  arm A   17.4  (first prefix)   |  16.2   11.7    9.7
  arm B   15.4   12.2    9.3
per-push latency, median / max seconds:
  arm A   1.66/7.51 (first)  |  1.70/11.70   2.36/7.65   2.95/7.87
  arm B   1.51/11.95   2.19/7.82   3.11/8.69

READING: the floor does not cost push rate. Both arms fall by the same shape as the branch
count grows (~900 new branches a minute; every push rewrites the snapshot's ref map), and the
arms cross over at repetition 2. Folds: arm A 50 in 1046 pushes (one per 21); arm B 12 in 2216
(one per 185), each firing at the 64-pack cap over 66-82 tier packs.

